{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>But the wicked, etc.</b> The sense is that HaShem will heal the righteous of Israel but not the wicked, for they are like the sea that is driven out constantly, as in ויגרשו מימיו (\"its waters were driven out\"), and close to the form of הנני גורש מפניך (Exodus 34:1)." "<b>for it cannot be still.</b> Meaning: like the sea [that is] driven out — behold, the word that is (נגרש) is missing, for נגרש is an adjective [describing] the noun." "<b>ויגרשו מימיו.</b> Like ינועו (\"they toss\")."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:02.385473450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}